          {
            "id": "judge_prompt",
            "type": "nodetool.text.Prompt",
            "data": {
              "prompt": "Brief:\n{{ BRIEF }}\n\nAudience & constraints:\n{{ CONTEXT }}\n\nThree anonymous analysts answered this brief. You do not know who wrote which answer.\n\n<answer id=\"A\">\n{{ ANSWER_A }}\n</answer>\n\n<answer id=\"B\">\n{{ ANSWER_B }}\n</answer>\n\n<answer id=\"C\">\n{{ ANSWER_C }}\n</answer>\n\nScore each answer from 1 to 5 on four criteria:\n- **Decisive:** commits to one clear recommendation.\n- **Grounded:** reasoning uses the stated constraints, not generic advice.\n- **Honest:** the counterargument is the strongest real one, not a strawman.\n- **Actionable:** a decision-maker could act on it tomorrow.\n\nAn empty or failed answer scores 0 on every criterion.\n\nReply in Markdown with exactly these sections and nothing else:\n\n## Scorecard\nA table with columns Answer, Decisive, Grounded, Honest, Actionable, Total.\n\n## Winner\nOne line: the winning answer's letter and the deciding reason.\n\n## What every answer missed\nOne short paragraph, or \"Nothing material.\""
            },
